<title>SPAIN: Spain July registered jobless at 16-year low.</title>
<headline>Spain July registered jobless at 16-year low.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish registered unemployment rate dropped to 12.5 percent in July, the first time since 1981 that it has fallen beneath 13 percent, the Labour Ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;This is the first time since 1981 that the rate has gone below 13 percent,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>In addition, the number of  job contracts registered in July reached 968,177, a record. Of those, 86,094 were indefinite, or permanent, the statment said.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
